# abbiey.search — Core Rules

## Project Overview
Privacy-first search engine built with Python/Flask on Vercel, backed by Supabase PostgreSQL.
Full context in `AGENTS.md` (architecture, integration IDs, recovery runbook).

## Stack
- Python 3.12 / Flask — `app.py` (~6,000 lines)
- Vanilla JS + Jinja2 — `static/script.js`, `templates/`
- PostgreSQL 17 via Supabase (project `xwxscvllmghyogddpmii`)
- Supabase Auth — Google OAuth (PKCE) + email/password
- Vercel serverless deployment

## CSP Nonce — CRITICAL RULE
**Every `<script>` tag in every template must have `nonce="{{ csp_nonce }}"`.**

```html
<!-- CORRECT -->
<script nonce="{{ csp_nonce }}">...</script>

<!-- WRONG — silently blocked in production -->
<script>...</script>
```

The nonce is generated per-request in `app.py` `@before_request` and injected via context processor.

## Python / Flask Rules
- Use `flask-limiter` decorators for rate-sensitive routes
- Admin endpoints: protected by `_admin_check()` — accepts `?token=` or `X-Admin-Token`
- Database: always use Transaction pooler (port 6543), never direct connection (port 5432)
- HTTP calls: use `_get_http()` helper (wraps `httpx`)
- No secrets in code — use env vars; reference `.env.example` for the full list

## Testing
```bash
pytest tests/ -v          # run full suite
pytest tests/test_app.py  # single file
```
Tests live in `tests/`; fixtures in `tests/conftest.py`.
